===Noun===
{{head|en|noun}}
{{rfc|en}}

# {{lb|en|US|slang}} Fifteen years.
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} after discount stores where “everything costs a nickel and dime”. 
Stores were common before 1950s in the USA. 
Stores in the 2000s commonly called “[[dollar store]]”s

# {{lb|en|US|and|Canada}} A [[retail]] store selling [[inexpensive]] items, especially one in which all items have a [[price]] near a [[nickle]] (US five cents) or a [[dime]] (US ten cents)

Alternatively called a [[five and ten]] or a [[five and dime]]

